ist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-21T20:51:50Z","updated_at":"2023-09-21T20:51:50Z","body":"Okay. We have to consider making it. But, it may be a breaking change. So will be included in the next major version \"v4\". Thanks!","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1730283843/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1812191216","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/1441#issuecomment-1812191216","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1441","id":1812191216,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM5sA9fw","user":{"login":"jvhellemond","id":968908,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2ODkwOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/968908?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond","html_url":"https://github.com/jvhellemond","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jvhellemond/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-11-15T10:27:08Z","updated_at":"2023-11-15T10:29:43Z","body":"+1\r\nI like to keep all my error responses uniform, with (translated) messages form malformed JSON or FormData generated by onError.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1812191216/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/3075827047","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/1441#issuecomment-3075827047","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1441","id":3075827047,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM63VWVn","user":{"login":"MonsterDeveloper","id":16190582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTkwNTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16190582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper","html_url":"https://github.com/MonsterDeveloper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MonsterDeveloper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-15T21:43:46Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T21:43:46Z","body":"@yusukebe I would suggest re-opening as the key issue is not solved: the validator just [returns the response](https://github.com/honojs/hono/blob/89f4c9691dd688d70e2b707fe87a8b97cb932136/src/validator/validator.ts#L141) from the validation function rather than `throw`-ing it:\n```ts\nconst res = await validationFunc(value as never, c as never)\nif (res instanceof Response) {\n  return res\n}\n```\n\nFrom me personally the request is to make `app.onError` a single entry-point for error handling, so all the errors returned from the API can have a standard shape, e.g.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"message\": \"You do not have permission to access this resource\",\n  \"type\": \"Unauthorized\",\n  \"types\": [\"Unauthorized\", \"Security\"],\n  \"cause\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\nCurrently in order to modify the shape of errors returned from the validators (`sValidator`, `zValidator`, etc) every call should have a `hook` that would throw the validation error/return a modified response.\n\nA solution might be a `shouldThrow` option passed to the validator, so the error can be handled in `app.onError`. Example:\n\n```ts\napp.post(\"/\",\n  sValidator(\"json\", z.object({}), { shouldThrow: true }),\n  async c => {\n    // ...\n  }\n)\n```\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/3075827047/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/3092654844","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/1441#issuecomment-3092654844","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1441","id":3092654844,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM64Vir8","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-20T00:30:20Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T00:30:20Z","body":"Hi @MonsterDeveloper \n\nI thought about that, but I think it's okay not to add the `shouldThrow` option since I don't want to introduce a breaking change. You can write the following to throw an error (right?).\n\n```ts\nimport { Hono } from 'hono'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { sValidator } from '@hono/standard-validator'\n\nconst schema = z.object({\n  name: z.string()\n})\n\nconst app = new Hono()\n\napp.get(\n  '/',\n  sValidator('query', schema, (data) => {\n    if (!data.success) {\n      throw new Error(JSON.stringify(data.error))\n    }\n  }),\n  async (c) => {\n    const { name } = c.req.valid('query')\n    return c.json({ name })\n  }\n)\n```\n\nThis code is not so long and is easy to understand what it does.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/3092654844/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/4246902134","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/1441#issuecomment-4246902134","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1441","id":4246902134,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM79IpV2","user":{"login":"ayZagen","id":11196940,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTk2OTQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11196940?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen","html_url":"https://github.com/ayZagen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ayZagen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T20:26:16Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T20:26:16Z","body":"hi @yusukebe, wouldn’t it be better to have a global option for this purpose? For such a feature, having to pass a parameter or function to each route validator seems like poor design. And this is really necessary to have.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/4246902134/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/4249151605","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/1441#issuecomment-4249151605","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1441","id":4249151605,"node_id":"IC_kwDO